Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 're'

Solution: The re module is built-in. Check Python version with python3 --version
Issue: Password input shows on screen

Solution: For production, use import getpass and getpass.getpass() instead of input()
Issue: File not found when loading common passwords

Solution: Verify file exists with ls -la common_passwords.txt and check file path
Issue: Regex patterns not matching

Solution: Test patterns individually using Python interactive mode: python3 then import re; re.search(r'[a-z]', 'Test')
